        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Tetrapolis (Attica), Attica, Marathon, Probalinthus, Tricorythus, Oenoe, Greece\n- Events: Battle of Marathon\n- Topics: ancient districts, ancient Greek cities\n\nFacts:\n- Tetrapolis (Attica) was a district on a plain in the northeastern part of Attica.\n- Tetrapolis (Attica) contained four cities: Marathon, Probalinthus, Tricorythus, and Oenoe.\n- In 490 BC, the Battle of Marathon took place at Marathon in Greece.\n- At the Battle of Marathon in 490 BC, the heavily outnumbered Athenian army defeated the Persians.\n- Marathon is a town in Greece.\n- Marathon is also known as Μαραθώνας in Demotic Greek and Μαραθών in Attic/Katharevousa.",
